    description: "WHAT, after PR #2200:\n- Not hashed by the current rule (owner's call; each MOVES IDS): constructor parameter types, getter and setter types, top-level variable types.\n- Methods of an unnamed extension have no owner, so two `ext()` in two unnamed extensions collide; methods of extension types and enums are bare-named.\n- Operators, factory constructors and typedefs are not emitted (extension type declarations: WI-volus-hidar-folod-hanoz-kumam-bahik-hogop-josad).\n\nMEASUREMENT LIMIT. Every Dart figure of the v15 history row comes from sub-trees of one clone (sherpa-onnx); no second Dart repository is on the machine.\n\nFixing a part marked MOVES IDS changes hashed input, so it belongs to the next stable-id bump, with a measured churn figure in the spec's history row.\n\nFound during PR 2 of the stable-id plan (the v15 bump), 2026-11-16 (PR #2200). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/STATUS.md."  # b6d1
